data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work with `stackalloc`:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

On this 64-bit system, each element is 8 bytes. The only quirk is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context (since the size isn't known at compile time), but you can use `nint.Size` instead.
